{# Decision template: which of an NPC's memories, if any, the player's line asks about, so that recall
   returns that memory alone. Rendered into a decisions request, never into chat messages. Sent when
   memory_retrieval.decision_gate.enabled is on; when the answer is none, too uncertain, or the request
   fails, recall falls back to its plain similarity search.

   Context set by the game: npc (UUID, name), player_line (the player's line, verbatim),
   recent_conversation (the lines before it, oldest first, "Speaker: line"), decision_memories
   (key, content: the memories that came closest to the line and to the conversation, key m1, m2, ...).
   The game accepts a memory when the probability that some memory applies (1 - p(none)) clears the
   configured cut-off, and takes the likeliest one; near-duplicate memories of one event may share the
   probability between them. Keys are per request; use m.key as given.

   A criterion is one line; the game flattens each memory's text to one line before it gets here. #}
[ state npc ]
{{ npc.name }}
[ end state ]

[ state player_line ]
{{ player_line }}
[ end state ]

[ state recent_conversation ]
{% if recent_conversation != "" %}{{ recent_conversation }}{% else %}(nothing was said before this line){% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ question memory choice ]
The player just said `player_line` to {{ npc.name }}, after the lines in `recent_conversation`. The options are memories of {{ npc.name }}'s that came closest to the line and to the conversation. Decide which memory, if any, the line asks about or refers to, so that {{ npc.name }} should recall it to answer; use the conversation to resolve what the line means (a short reply, a follow-up question, a "what about that" refers to what was just being talked about).
Pick a memory only when the line is about the event, person or thing in it. A name or place in the line that a memory shares is a strong sign when the line asks about the past.
Choose none when the line refers to none of them, or to something happening right now rather than the past: a greeting, a request, a remark about the present scene, a question about {{ npc.name }}'s opinion of something no memory covers.
[ criteria ]
{% for m in decision_memories %}
{{ m.key }}: {{ m.content }}
{% endfor %}
none: No offered memory fits: the line is about the present, or about something none of these memories covers.
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
